    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes high-upside speed and favorable platoon matchups against middle-of-the-road arms. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) represent our most potent offensive engines; **James Wood** benefits from a high-volume matchup against Chandler and an elite base-stealing environment, while **Mickey Moniak** receives a massive +14% boost from a favorable platoon split and a prime spot in the #2 hole against Mahle. **Brice Turang** (75.06) remains a must-start, leveraging his leadoff status and the aggressive base-running opportunities presented by Rodriguez\u2019s slow delivery, effectively mitigating his negative platoon split against the southpaw. **Corbin Carroll** (72.02) rounds out our core, though we are tempering expectations slightly due to the \"Elite Hold\" status of Sproat, which dampens his SB ceiling.\n\nRegarding lineup construction, the most difficult decision involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 52.23 score. While his leadoff projection is attractive, his struggle against southpaws (a -9% platoon penalty) proved fatal against Murphy, allowing the more stable, high-floor output of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** to hold their spots. We are also keeping a close eye on **Max Muncy** (55.43); while he offers a +10% park boost, his position in the #7 spot and his neutralized platoon matchup suggest he is a marginal play today. **Alex Freeland** is the primary high-variance wildcard; while his #8 order placement is a anchor, the +19% SP skill bonus and +5% wind-assisted boost make him a sneaky asset if he can capitalize on the favorable matchup against Sears. No severe weather risks are currently impacting the roster, but managers should note that any shift in the wind direction in the **Alex Freeland** game could necessitate a late swap if it turns against his power profile.",
